<title>NETHERLANDS: Oce says no provision for antitrust action.</title>
<headline>Oce says no provision for antitrust action.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Printer and copier maker Oce- van der Grinten said on Monday it had made no provisions for the outcome of a U.S. lawsuit filed against companies including Siemens Nixdorf Printing (SNI), which it acquired last year.</p>
<p>&quot;We have made no provision for the class action...there is no point in making one,&quot; Oce chairman Harry Pennings told a news conference on the firm's results.</p>
<p>Several service companies filed a class action last November alleging violations of Florida anti-trust laws against various Siemens units, AT&amp;T Corp Global Information Solutions and Oce Printing Systems USA (formerly Siemens Nixdorf Printing).</p>
<p>Pennings said the suit related to incidents which, if proven, had occurred before Oce acquired the Siemens activities.</p>
<p>In the unlikely event of the claim being upheld, Oce could not be held liable, Pennings said.</p>
